// REJECTS: Unexpected token '~mainTable'
//
// `~mainTable` is a relational CLASS MAPPING modifier. A View has no such clause: its
// source tables come from the columns it projects, and its only modifiers are ~filter,
// ~groupBy and ~distinct.
//
// This is the same trap as ordering-view-modifiers.pure seen from the other side. The two
// constructs share three modifier spellings out of five, so a rewrite that factors "parse
// the ~-clauses" into one routine gets a View that accepts ~mainTable and ~primaryKey and a
// class mapping that accepts them in the View's order. Neither engine would agree with it.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::ViewMainTable
(
   Table T (ID VARCHAR(32) PRIMARY KEY, VAL VARCHAR(32))
   View V
   (
      ~mainTable [fixture::neg::ViewMainTable]T
      id: T.ID PRIMARY KEY,
      val: T.VAL
   )
)
